#  Object-Oriented Programming (OOP)

## What is OOPS
OOP (Object-Oriented Programming) System is a programming paradigm based on objects and classes,
used to design programs in a structured and reusable way.



##  Core Concepts of OOP

* Encapsulation → Wrapping data + methods together
* Inheritance → Acquiring properties of another class
* Polymorphism → One action, many forms
* Abstraction → Hiding implementation details



##  Class

A class is a blueprint/template used to create objects.

It has -
* Variables (data / properties)
* Methods (behavior / functions)

### Syntax

class ClassName {
    // variables
    // methods
}


##  Object
An object is an instance of a class.

### Syntax
ClassName obj = new ClassName();



## Example (Class & Object)

class Student {
    String name;
    int age;

    void display() {
        System.out.println(name + " " + age);
    }
}


public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Student s1 = new Student();
        s1.name = "Aarzoo";
        s1.age = 20;

        s1.display();
    }
}

